--TEST--
a class-scoped `type` alias naming one class-shaped atom on its own is `E0307`, in a class, an interface and an enum body alike — `rule:types/alias-is-never-a-bare-class`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/alias-is-never-a-bare-class`: an alias names a type expression,
// and a single class-shaped atom on its own is the one production it may not
// name — a class already has a name, and a second one for it is what
// `rule:statements/nothing-gets-a-second-name` refuses. A class-scoped alias
// is the same declaration in a different body, so it is the same refusal, in
// a class, an interface and an enum body alike.
class Thing {}
interface Contract {}
enum Colour: int {
    Red = 1,
}

// The accepted half first: the atom is refused bare, not wherever it appears.
// A union, an intersection and a wrapper each name a shape the class does not
// already have a name for, and a parenthesised atom is not the bare form.
class Accepted {
    type OrNull = Thing|null;
    type Both = Thing&Contract;
    type Many = array<Thing>;
    type Wrapped = (Colour);
}

class OfAClass {
    type Id = Thing;
}

interface OfAnInterface {
    type Id = Contract;
}

enum OfAnEnum: int {
    On = 1,

    type Id = Colour;
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0307]: a `type` alias may not name a single class, interface or enum on its own
   --> case.nvs:25:15
%A
error[E0307]: a `type` alias may not name a single class, interface or enum on its own
   --> case.nvs:29:15
%A
error[E0307]: a `type` alias may not name a single class, interface or enum on its own
   --> case.nvs:35:15
%A
